Recommend `selected: Id | null` as a required CategoryWheel prop and `$state<RankingCategory | null>(null)` on `/rankings`. Null represents precisely one additional state: no category chosen. Keep `onselect: (id: Id) => void`; clicking a selected category remains selected. A tagged `{ kind: 'initial' } | { kind: 'selected'; category: RankingCategory }` adds ceremony without enforcing any additional invariant here. Reserve it for future states with associated data.

Guard `rankingRows` with `data.rankings && selected !== null`, and guard the entire board with `selected !== null`. Initial UI contains the heading, subtitle “All donations for this parliamentary term”, and wheel; it contains no list, empty-results message, or party context. Every button starts `aria-pressed="false"`. After selection, preserve current category-specific subtitle, party context, rows, and empty-results behavior. Server preloading and backend calculations remain unchanged.

Move the existing 13% accent tint from `path.selected` into the ordinary sector path rule. Keep selected styling limited to an accent stroke/rim; remove selection-mark markup and its CSS. Remove pressed label recoloring if the rim should be the sole selection indicator. Preserve member purple, funder teal, neutral parties, and muted utility icons. Keep the independent 6px neutral focus outline and native button keyboard behavior. Explicit focus rules must retain `fill: none`.

Existing gallery callers passing a concrete ID remain compatible; add an unselected example and verify initial absence of a board, first selection, switching, aria-pressed, constant fills, and visible keyboard focus. Financial labels and all totals remain unchanged.
Recommend `selected: Id | null` (still a required prop) on `CategoryWheel`; page state becomes `$state<RankingCategory | null>(null)`. This exactly represents the two real states without an extra discriminator. A tagged `{ kind: "initial" } | { kind: "selected"; category: RankingCategory }` adds matching and projection but protects no additional invariant: selection has no associated lifecycle data or effects.

Keep `onselect: (id: Id) => void`: selecting a category always yields a valid identity, and clicking it again leaves it selected. No deselection action is requested. With null, every native button has `aria-pressed=false`; keyboard activation selects normally.

On `/rankings`, derive rows only when both `data.rankings` exists and `selected !== null`. Render the entire `.board` only under `selected !== null`, including party context and empty message. Initial subtitle remains exactly “All donations for this parliamentary term”; members retain “All declared amounts for this parliamentary term” after selection. Existing preloaded server data and row formatting remain unchanged.

Move the existing tinted fill from `path.selected` to the normal sector path rule, retaining each option’s member/funder/neutral accent. Selection changes only the accent rim; remove the check span and its CSS. Keep the independent neutral focus-outline path, its thicker stroke visible outside the selected rim. Preserve muted utility icons.

The gallery can keep its current explicit selection; update its documented contract to nullable selection, permanent tint, and rim indication. Verify initial absence of rankings/empty message, activation for all categories, constant fills across selection, no tick, and separate keyboard focus.
Recommend `selected: Id | null` for the reusable wheel. The state is genuinely optional; a tagged `initial | selected` union adds a second representation of the same absence and makes every consumer branch twice. Keep `onselect(id)` unchanged. `null` means no pressed sector, no selected rim, and no list; a chosen ID means exactly one pressed sector and its rim.

On `/rankings`, initialize to `null`. Render the existing “All donations for this parliamentary term” subtitle and omit the board/list until a choice. After a click, show that category’s rows and existing contextual text. Derive rows only when both server data and selected ID exist; do not change server preload or ranking conversion.

Wheel styling should keep every sector’s accent tint permanently: derive fill from `data-accent` (member purple, funder teal, party neutral) regardless of selection. Selection changes only the sector’s rim/stroke and `aria-pressed`; remove the check mark and selected label-color shift. Preserve `:focus-visible` as an independent neutral outline, including when a selected sector has keyboard focus.

The design-system gallery must pass an initial `null` selection or its chosen example ID; document the nullable contract in the component README. This keeps the generic API small while letting the page model initial versus chosen content explicitly.
